n la exploraci\u00f3n del tema.\n\nContexto recuperado (puede estar vac\u00edo; t\u00f3malo en cuenta solo si aporta informaci\u00f3n relevante para la evaluaci\u00f3n):\nse proporciona en el campo Retrieval Context.\n\nDevuelve la puntuaci\u00f3n y una justificaci\u00f3n breve en espa\u00f1ol. \n \nEvaluation Steps:\n[\n    \"Revisa el Input para identificar el tema o pregunta principal y el nivel de profundidad esperado.\",\n    \"Analiza el Actual Output y eval\u00faa si la respuesta explora el tema con argumentos, explicaciones o ejemplos detallados que demuestren un an\u00e1lisis profundo.\",\n    \"Considera el Retrieval Context (si existe) y verifica si la respuesta incorpora informaci\u00f3n relevante del contexto para enriquecer el an\u00e1lisis.\",\n    \"Compara la respuesta con el Input y el Retrieval Context para determinar si la profundidad anal\u00edtica es suficiente, insuficiente o sobresaliente seg\u00fan lo requerido.\"\n] \n \nRubric:\n0-2: An\u00e1lisis m\u00ednimo o inexistente; respuesta superficial\n3-4: An\u00e1lisis superficial; mayormente respuestas de nivel b\u00e1sico\n5-6: An\u00e1lisis moderado; algunos aspectos explorados superficialmente\n7-8: An\u00e1lisis s\u00f3lido con exploraci\u00f3n adecuada de aspectos clave\n9-10: An\u00e1lisis profundo y perspicaz; explora m\u00faltiples dimensiones del problema"}], "runDuration": 11.03108941699611, "evaluationCost": 0.48411799999999994}, {"name": "test_rag_quality[openai:gpt-5.6-sol-If First Mint's Nevada facilities expand, how does PPE vs. derecognized mine asset classification shift in 2023?-In 2023, First Mint\\u2019s property, plant and equipment (PPE) in Nevada was included in \"Other\" at $51.8 million, but by 2024 this decreased to $3.1 million. Meanwhile, non-producing mines like La Guitarra and La Parrilla were classified as assets held-for-sale until their disposal, after which their assets and liabilities were derecognized as of December 31, 2023. Therefore, if First Mint\\u2019s Nevada facilities expand, their PPE would increase and appear in \"Other,\" while derecognized mine assets would not be reflected on the balance sheet, demonstrating a shift from derecognition of sold mines to increased PPE from ongoing Nevada operations.-(3) Included in \"Other\" is property, plant and equipment of $3.1 million (2023 51.8 million) for First Mint which includes the Company's bullion store and its minting facility located in Nevada\\n\\nProperty, plant and equipment, including land and buildings, machinery and equipment; assets under construction and other assets above are allocated by mine as follow:\\n\\n<invoke name=\"Read\">\\n<parameter name=\"file_path\">/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-jmanuelc87-Documents-Companies-Cognitactix-grupo-mexico-evals/dde52c23-b3a0-4425-a3ab-62404ca21536/images/1.png</parameter>\\n</invoke>\\nalt\\n\\n\\n<invoke name=\"Read\">\\n<parameter name=\"file_path\">/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-jmanuelc87-Documents-Companies-Cognitactix-grupo-mexico-evals/dde52c23-b3a0-4425-a3ab-62404ca21536/images/1.png</parameter>\\n</invoke>\\nalt\\n\\nTabular amounts are expressed in thousands of US dollars)\\n\\nPage\\n\\nNOTES TO CONDENSED INTERIM CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS\\n\\nFirst Majestic Silver Corp. 2024 First Quarter Report\\n\\n(1) Non-producing properties include the San Martin, Del Toro, La Parrilla and La Guitarra mines. La Guitarra and La Parrilla were classified as assets held-for- sale up to the date of disposition on March 29, 2023 and August 14, 2023, respectively. As of December 31, 2023, the assets and liabilities have been derecognized\\n\\nThe accompanying notes are an integral part of the condensed interim consolidated financial statements\\n\\nCondensed Interim Consolidated Financial Statements Unaudited\\n]", "input": "If First Mint's Nevada facilities expand, how does PPE vs. derecognized mine asset classification shift in 2023?", "actualOutput": "An expansion of First Mint\u2019s Nevada bullion store or minting facility would increase **PPE**, initially potentially within **assets under construction**, rather than create a mineral-property asset. First Mint\u2019s facilities were already reported as **$1.8 million of PPE within \u201cOther\u201d at December 31, 2023** [FSMDA-Q1-2024 p.24].\n\nThis is separate from the 2023 mine disposals: La Guitarra and La Parrilla were held for sale until their March and August 2023 sales, after which their assets and liabilities were **derecognized** [FSMDA-Q2-2024 p.25]. Those disposals removed **$48.0 million of mineral-property interests** and **$9.8 million of PPE** in aggregate [FSMDA-Q1-2024 p.19].\n\nThus, the classification shift is toward **more continuing PPE for First Mint**, while derecognition applies only to the sold mine assets\u2014not to an expansion of the Nevada mint. The documents do not quantify a hypothetical expansion\u2019s 2023 amount.", "expectedOutput": "In 2023, First Mint\u2019s property, plant and equipment (PPE) in Nevada was included in \"Other\" at $51.8 million, but by 2024 this decreased to $3.1 million. Meanwhile, non-producing mines like La Guitarra and La Parrilla were classified as assets held-for-sale until their disposal, after which their assets and liabilities were derecognized as of December 31, 2023. Therefore, if First Mint\u2019s Nevada facilities expand, their PPE would increase and appear in \"Other,\" while derecognized mine assets would not be reflected on the balance sheet, demonstrating a shift from derecognition of sold mines to increased PPE from ongoing Nevada operations.", "context": ["(3) Included in \"Other\" is property, plant and equipment of $3.1 million (2023 51.8 million) for First Mint which includes the Company's bullion store and its minting facility located in Nevada\n\nProperty, plant and equipment, including land and buildings, machinery and equipment; assets under construction and other assets above are allocated by mine as follow:\n\n<invoke name=\"Read