ed mine asset into PPE because of First Mint\u2019s Nevada expansion. What the documents show is:\n\n- **First Mint\u2019s Nevada bullion store and minting facility were classified as PPE** and, for 2023 comparatives, were included in **\u201cOther\u201d** rather than as a separate segment. The reported PPE for First Mint was **$1.8 million at December 31, 2023** (shown in 2024 interim disclosures as \u201c2023 $1.8 million\u201d). [FSMDA-Q3-2024 p.25]\n- **Beginning January 1, 2024, First Mint became a separate significant segment**, and prior-period information was reclassified from **\u201cOthers\u201d** into the **First Mint** segment for presentation purposes. [FSMDA-Q1-2024 p.11] [FSMDA-Q2-2024 p.11] [FSMDA-Q3-2024 p.11]\n- The filings separately say **Jerritt Canyon** in Nevada was put on **temporary suspension in March 2023** to focus on exploration, resource definition, and optimization of mine planning and plant operations, but the passages retrieved do **not** say that a \u201cderecognized mine asset\u201d was reclassified into First Mint PPE. [FSMDA-Q1-2024 p.11] [FSMDA-Q3-2024 p.11]\n\nSo, if First Mint\u2019s Nevada facilities expand, the evidence here suggests the accounting effect would be an **increase in PPE within the First Mint segment**; however, the documents retrieved do **not** support a specific 2023 shift from **derecognized mine asset** classification to **PPE**. They only support a **segment presentation change** from **\u201cOthers\u201d** to **\u201cFirst Mint\u201d** in 2024, with 2023 comparative First Mint assets already sitting in PPE. [FSMDA-Q3-2024 p.25] [FSMDA-Q1-2024 p.11]\n\nIf you want, I can also look specifically for the note on **asset derecognition/impairment at Jerritt Canyon** to see whether that is what your question is referring to.", "expectedOutput": "In 2023, First Mint\u2019s property, plant and equipment (PPE) in Nevada was included in \"Other\" at $51.8 million, but by 2024 this decreased to $3.1 million. Meanwhi