,357 (\u221248%)** |\n| **Total assets** | **1,979,788** | **1,976,355** | **+3,433** |\n\nTotal assets were essentially flat; the mix shifted toward current assets (cash up ~61%) while non-current assets fell, driven by lower PP&E, restricted cash, and especially deferred tax assets [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.11].\n\n## Liabilities\n\n| | Dec 31, 2024 | Dec 31, 2023 | Change |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Trade and other payables | 103,895 | 94,413 | +9,482 |\n| Unearned revenue | 580 | 2,301 | \u22121,721 |\n| Current debt facilities | 825 | 832 | \u22127 |\n| Current lease liabilities | 16,215 | 17,370 | \u22121,155 |\n| Income taxes payable | 22,792 | 5,222 | +17,570 |\n| **Total current liabilities** | **144,307** | **120,138** | **+24,169 (+20%)** |\n| Debt facilities | 208,657 | 218,980 | \u221210,323 |\n| Lease liabilities | 11,320 | 19,332 | \u22128,012 |\n| Decommissioning liabilities | 159,067 | 151,564 | +7,503 |\n| Other liabilities | 5,587 | 5,592 | \u22125 |\n| Non-current income taxes payable | 19,685 | 23,612 | \u22123,927 |\n| **Deferred tax liabilities** | **80,094** | **79,017** | **+1,077** |\n| **Total liabilities** | **628,717** | **618,235** | **+10,482 (+1.7%)** |\n\nCurrent liabilities rose mainly from higher income taxes payable and payables; non\u2011current liabilities declined modestly as debt and lease liabilities were paid down, partly offset by higher decommissioning provisions [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.11].\n\n## Equity\n\n| | Dec 31, 2024 | Dec 31, 2023 | Change |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Share capital | 1,978,101 | 1,879,971 | +98,130 |\n| Equity reserves | 90,028 | 88,025 | +2,003 |\n| Accumulated deficit | (717,058) | (609,876) | \u2212107,182 |\n| **Total equity** | **1,351,071** | **1,358,120** | **\u22127,049 (\u22120.5%)** |\n| Total liabilities and equity | 1,979,788 | 1,976,355 | +3,433 |\n\nShare issuance of ~US$98 million was almost entirely absorbed by a US$107 million increase in the accumulated deficit, leaving equity slightly lower [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.11].\n\n## Deferred taxes in detail\n\n- **Net position**: net deferred tax asset of US$9.7 million at end\u20112023 (DTA 88,732 \u2212 DTL 79,017) swung to a **net deferred tax liability of US$33.7 million** at end\u20112024 (DTA 46,375 \u2212 DTL 80,094) [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.58].\n- **Gross deferred tax assets** (before offsetting) rose from 136,020 to 141,794: tax losses +35,406 and provisions +2,043, partly offset by a larger unrecognized DTA (\u221228,715; from \u2212130,613 to \u2212159,328) and other (\u22122,960) [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.58].\n- **Gross deferred tax liabilities** rose from 126,304 to 175,513, driven by PP&E/mining interests (+58,576, to 188,517), partly offset by \"other\" (\u22129,367) [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.58].\n- The company recognized US$46.4 million (2023: US$88.7 million) of net DTAs in entities with tax losses in 2024 and/or 2023, based on budgets, forecasts and tax planning [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.58].\n\nIf you need Grupo M\u00e9xico's own balance sheet (e.g., from its annual report or 20\u2011F style financials), those statements are not in the current document set \u2014 I can only confirm the divisional tangible-asset and economic-value figures cited above.", "expectedOutput": "Between December 31, 2023, and December 31, 2024:\n\n**Current Assets** increased from $309,057 to $368,821, mainly due to higher cash and cash equivalents (up $76,599) and trade/other receivables (up $2,204), partially offset by lower inventories (down $1,166) and other financial assets (down $12,599).\n\n**Non-Current Assets** remained relatively stable, moving from $1,667,298 to $1,610,967. Key changes include an increase in mining interests (up $35,687), a decrease in property, plant, and equipment (down $27,664), and a drop in deferred tax assets (down $42,357).\n\n**Total Assets** stayed stable, rising slightly from $1,976,355 to $1,979,788.\n\n**Current Liabilities** increased from $120,138 to $144,307, driven mainly by higher trade and other payables (up $9,482) and income taxes payable (up $17,570).\n\n**Non-Current Liabilities** grew from $498,097 to $484,410. Notable movements include a decrease in debt facilities (down $10,323), a decrease in lease liabilities (down $8,012), and an increase in decommissioning liabilities (up $7,503).\n\n**Total Liabilities** rose from $618,235 to $628,717.\n\n**Equity** decreased from $1,358,120 to $1,351,071. This reflects an increase in share capital (up $98,130) and equity reserves (up $2,003), offset by a higher accumulated deficit (increase of $107,182).\n\n**Deferred Tax Assets** dropped from $88,732 to $46,375, while **Deferred Tax Liabilities** increased slightly from $79,017 to $80,094.\n\n**Summary:**  \n- Current assets and liabilities increased.  \n- Non-current asset and liability changes varied by category.  \n- Total assets and liabilities were relatively stable, but equity declined due to the increased deficit.  \n- Deferred tax assets decreased significantly; deferred tax liabilities grew slightly.", "context": ["| | Note | December 31, 2024 | December 31, 2023 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Assets** | | | |\n| **Current assets** | | | |\n| Cash and cash equivalents | | $202,180 | $125,581 |\n| Trade and other receivables | | 12,303 | 10,099 |\n| Value added taxes receivable | 26(c) | 33,864 | 38,587 |\n| Inventories | 12 | 62,524 | 63,690 |\n| Other financial assets | 13 | 49,781 | 62,380 |\n| Prepaid expenses and other | | 8,169 | 8,720 |\n| **Total current assets** | | **368,821** | **309,057** |\n| **Non-current assets** | | | |\n| Mining interests | 15 | 1,034,522 | 998,835 |\n| Property, plant and equipment | 16 | 378,630 | 406,294 |\n| Right-of-use assets | 17 | 23,898 | 27,284 |\n| Deposits on non-current assets | | 5,720 | 6,430 |\n| Trade and other receivables | | 5,000 | \u2014 |\n| Non-current restricted cash | 19 | 106,072 | 125,573 |\n| Non-current value added taxes receivable | 26(c) | 10,750 | 14,150 |\n| Deferred tax assets | 24 | 46,375 | 88,732 |\n| **To