lion [IDS24_ESP_03_Valor_Compartido_ebook p.13]. They don't split assets and liabilities into current and non-current or show deferred taxes.\n\nBelow is the comparison using First Majestic's figures, in thousands of US dollars, at December 31 of each year.\n\n## Assets [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.11]\n| | 2024 | 2023 | Change |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Current assets** | 368,821 | 309,057 | **+59,764 (+19.3%)** |\n| **Non-current assets** (total assets minus current) | 1,610,967 | 1,667,298 | **\u221256,331 (\u22123.4%)** |\n| **Total assets** | 1,979,788 | 1,976,355 | +3,433 |\n\n- **Current assets:** Cash and cash equivalents grew most (+76,599, from 125,581 to 202,180). Other financial assets (\u221212,599), VAT receivable (\u22124,723) and inventories (\u22121,166) went down.\n- **Non-current assets:** Mining interests rose (+35,687, to 1,034,522), and there was a new 5,000 long-term receivable. These were outweighed by lower deferred tax assets (\u221242,357), property, plant and equipment (\u221227,664), restricted cash (\u221219,501), non-current VAT (\u22123,400) and right-of-use assets (\u22123,386).\n\n## Liabilities [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.11]\n| | 2024 | 2023 | Change |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Current liabilities** | 144,307 | 120,138 | **+24,169 (+20.1%)** |\n| **Non-current liabilities** (total minus current) | 484,410 | 498,097 | **\u221213,687 (\u22122.7%)** |\n| **Total liabilities** | 628,717 | 618,235 | +10,482 |\n\n- **Current liabilities:** Income taxes payable rose (+17,570, from 5,222 to 22,792), as did trade payables (+9,482).\n- **Non-current liabilities:** Debt facilities fell (\u221210,323, to 208,657), along with lease liabilities (\u22128,012) and non-current taxes payable (\u22123,927). Decommissioning liabilities partly offset this (+7,503, to 159,067).\n- **Working capital** (current assets minus current liabilities) rose from 188,919 [FSMDA-Q1-2024 p.89] to about 224,514 (my calculation).\n\n## Equity [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.11]\n| | 2024 | 2023 | Change |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Share capital | 1,978,101 | 1,879,971 | +98,130 |\n| Equity reserves | 90,028 | 88,025 | +2,003 |\n| Accumulated deficit | (717,058) | (609,876) | \u2212107,182 |\n| **Total equity** | **1,351,071** | **1,358,120** | **\u22127,049 (\u22120.5%)** |\n\nNew shares issued roughly offset the larger accumulated deficit, so total equity changed little.\n\n## Deferred taxes [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.58]\n| As shown on the balance sheet | 2024 | 2023 | Change |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Deferred tax assets | 46,375 | 88,732 | \u221242,357 (\u221247.7%) |\n| Deferred tax liabilities | 80,094 | 79,017 | +1,077 (+1.4%) |\n| **Net position** | **33,719 net liability** | **9,715 net asset** | **swing of ~43,434** |\n\n- **Before offsetting** (gross figures in the tax note): deferred tax assets went from 136,020 to 141,794 (+5,774). Deferred tax liabilities went from 126,304 to 175,513 (+49,209). Most of that increase came from property, plant and equipment and mining interests (+58,576, to 188,517).\n- **Assets not recognized:** Deferred tax assets that weren't recognized grew from (130,613) to (159,328). That's why recognized assets rose only slightly even though tax losses increased (+35,406, to 238,014).\n- All recognized deferred tax assets (46.4M in 2024, 88.7M in 2023) sit in entities that had a tax loss in 2024, 2023 or both. Recognizing them depends on budgets, forecasts and tax planning.\n\n**Summary:** For First Majestic, the balance shifted from non-current to current assets, mainly because cash grew and deferred tax assets and restricted cash fell. Current liabilities rose with income taxes and payables, while long-term debt and leases went down. The deferred tax position flipped from a net asset to a net liability. If you have Grupo M\u00e9xico's audited financial statements, I can do the same analysis for the right company.", "expectedOutput": "Between December 31, 2023, and December 31, 2024:\n\n**Current Assets** increased from $309,057 to $368,821, ma