anies-Cognitactix-grupo-mexico-evals/dde52c23-b3a0-4425-a3ab-62404ca21536/images/1.png</parameter>\\n</invoke>\\nalt\\n\\n\\n<invoke name=\"Read\">\\n<parameter name=\"file_path\">/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-jmanuelc87-Documents-Companies-Cognitactix-grupo-mexico-evals/dde52c23-b3a0-4425-a3ab-62404ca21536/images/1.png</parameter>\\n</invoke>\\nalt\\n\\nTabular amounts are expressed in thousands of US dollars)\\n\\nPage\\n\\nNOTES TO CONDENSED INTERIM CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS\\n\\nFirst Majestic Silver Corp. 2024 First Quarter Report\\n\\n(1) Non-producing properties include the San Martin, Del Toro, La Parrilla and La Guitarra mines. La Guitarra and La Parrilla were classified as assets held-for- sale up to the date of disposition on March 29, 2023 and August 14, 2023, respectively. As of December 31, 2023, the assets and liabilities have been derecognized\\n\\nThe accompanying notes are an integral part of the condensed interim consolidated financial statements\\n\\nCondensed Interim Consolidated Financial Statements Unaudited\\n]", "input": "If First Mint's Nevada facilities expand, how does PPE vs. derecognized mine asset classification shift in 2023?", "actualOutput": "I can't answer this as a prediction, because none of the documents look at how a First Mint expansion would affect asset classification. Also, First Mint isn't a Grupo Mexico asset. The passages come from **First Majestic Silver Corp.'s** quarterly and annual reports, which are in the document set. Taken at face value, though, they show the two items are separate, so one wouldn't \"shift\" into the other.\n\n**1. First Mint is recorded as property, plant and equipment (PPE)**\n- First Mint, LLC is First Majestic's wholly owned minting facility in Nevada. Its sales started in March 2024 and it formally opened in September 2024 [FSMDA-Q3-2024 p.54; 2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.82].\n- Its PPE, which includes the bullion store and the mint, sits in the \"Other\" column of the PPE-by-mine table. The 2023 figure was **$1.8 million**. It rose to $3.1M in Q1 2024, $3.4M in Q2 and **$4.1M in Q3 2024** [FSMDA-Q1-2024 p.24; FSMDA-Q2-2024 p.25; FSMDA-Q3-2024 p.25].\n- New construction is recorded at cost as \"assets under construction.\" It moves into land and buildings, machinery and equipment, or other once it's ready to use [FSMDA-Q2-2024 p.24]. So the documents imply that any First Mint expansion would add to PPE, which is the pattern of the 2024 increases.\n\n**2. The mines removed from the books (derecognized) in 2023 are an unrelated event**\n- La Guitarra and La Parrilla were held for sale and then sold, on March 29, 2023 and August 14, 2023. At December 31, 2023 their assets and liabilities had been taken off the books [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.44].\n- La Guitarra went to Sierra Madre with a carrying value of **$34.3M** at disposal. The sale produced a **$1.4M loss** [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.42].\n- La Parrilla went to Silver Storm Mining. Its net carrying value was **$56.4M** at December 31, 2022. Its liabilities stayed with First Majestic because the deal was a sale of assets [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.76].\n- In 2023 First Majestic also booked a **$125.2M impairment** (an accounting write-down). That splits into $78.1M on producing mining interests, $17.4M on exploration properties and $29.7M on PPE [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.50]. The passage doesn't say which mines it applied to.\n\n**In short:** the PPE growth from First Mint and the 2023 mine sales are separate accounting events, and growing First Mint wouldn't change how the sold mines were treated. In 2023 itself, First Mint's PPE was small ($1.8M) next to the roughly $90M of mine assets that were sold off. The documents don't model how classification would change if First Mint kept growing.\n\nIf you meant a Grupo Mexico asset instead, such as Southern Copper or ASARCO, tell me which one and I'll search for it.", "expectedOutput": "In 2023, First Mint\u2019s property, plant and equipment (PPE) in Nevada was included in \"Other\" at $51.8 million, but by 2024 this decreased to $3.1 million. Meanwhile, non-producing mines like La Guitarra and La Parrilla were classified as assets held-for-sale until their disposal, after which their assets and liabilities were derecognized as of December 31, 2023. Therefore, if First Mint\u2019s Nevada facilities expand, their PPE would increase and appear in \"Other,\" while derecognized mine assets would not be reflected on the balance sheet, demonstrating a shift from derecognition of sold mines to increased PPE from ongoing Nevada operations.", "context": ["(3) Included in \"Other\" is property, plant and equipment of $3.1 million (2023 51.8 million) for First Mint which includes the Company's bullion store and its minting facility located in Nevada\n\nProperty, plant and equipment, including land and buildings, machinery and equipment; assets under construction and other assets above are allocated by mine as follow:\n\n<invoke name=\"Read\">\n<parameter name=\"file_path\">/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-jmanuelc87-Documents-Companies-Cognitactix-grupo-mexico-evals/dde52c23-b3a0-4425-a3ab-62404ca21536/images/1.png</parameter>\n</invoke>\nalt\n\n\n<invoke name=\"Read\">\n<parameter name=\"file_path\">/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-jmanuelc87-Documents-Companies-Cognitactix-grupo-mexico-evals/dde52c23-b3a0-4425-a3ab-62404ca21536/images/1.png</parameter>\n</invoke>\nalt\n\nTabular amounts are expressed in thousands of US dollars)\n\nPage\n\nNOTES TO CONDENSED INTERIM CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS\n\nFirst Majestic Silver Corp. 2024 First Quarter Report\n\n(1) Non-producing properties include the San Martin, Del Toro, La Parrilla and La Guitarra mines. La Guitarra and La Parrilla were classified as assets held-for- sale up to the date of disposition on March 29, 2023 and August 14, 2023, respectively. As of December 31, 2023, the assets and liabilities have been derecognized\n\nThe accompanying notes are an integral part of the condensed interim consolidated financial statements\n\nCondensed Interim Consolidated Financial Statements Unaudited\n"], "retrievalContext": ["First Mint(1)\n\nFirst Majestic Silver Corp. 2024 Third Quarter Report\n\nFirst Mint, LLC (\"First Mint\") is the Company's operating minting facility located in Nevada, United States. First Mint expands upon the Company's existing bullion sales through vertically integrating the production of investment- grade fine silver bullion and allows the Company to sell a greater portion of its silver production directly to its shareholders and bullion customers First  Mint operates some of the most innovative processing equipment in the precious metals industry, including an environmentally friendly flameless tunnel, which is a zero-emission facility and uses significantly less electricity when compared to traditional minting processes_ This will enable the Company to turn its own silver into an array of finished bullion products, as well as offer manufacturing capacity for third-party demand. The Company owns 100% of First Mint, LLC", "First Mint, LLC 'First Mint\") is the Company's operating minting facility located in Nevada, United States. First Mint expands upon the Company's existing bullion sales through vertically integrating the production of investment-grade fine silver bullion, and the Company expects that First Mint will allow the Company to sell greater portion of its silver production directly to its shareholders and bullion customers. First Mint operates some of the most innovative processing equipment in the precious metals industry, including an environmentally friendly flameless tunnel, which uses significantly less electricity and produces near zero emissions when compared to traditional minting processes. First Mint enables the Company to turn its own silver into an array of finished bullion products, and provides manufacturing capacity for third-party demand. The Company owns 100% of First Mint.\n\n2024 Q4 vs. 2024 Q3", "First Mint LLC (\"First Mint\") is the Company's operating minting facility located in Nevada, United States. First Mint expands upon the Company's existing bullion sales through vertically integrating the production of investment-e grade fine silver bullion and allows the Company to sell a greater portion of its silver production directly to its shareholders and bullion customers- First Mint operates some of the most innovative processing equipment in the precious metals industry, including an environmentally friendly flameless tunnel, which uses significantly less electricity and releases fewer emissions when compared to traditional minting processes_ This will enable the Company to turn its own silver into an array of finished bullion products, as well as offer manufacturing capacity for third-party demand. The Company owns 100% of First Mint LLC.", "First Mint(2)\n\nFirst Majestic Silver Corp. 2024 Second Quarter Report\n\nFirst Mint LLC (\"First Mint\") is the Company's operating minting facility located in Nevada, United States. First Mint expands upon the Company's existing bullion sales through vertically integrating the production of investment-e grade fine silver bullion and allows the Company to sell a greater portion of its silver production directly to its shareholders and bullion customers- First Mint operates some of the most innovative processing equipment in the precious metals industry, including an environmentally friendly flameless tunnel, which is a zero-emission facility and uses significantly less electricity when compared to traditional minting processes_ This will enable the Company to turn its own silver into an array of finished bullion products, as well as offer manufacturing capacity for third-party demand. The Company owns 100% of First Mint LLC.\n\nConsider the chunked-reasoning...\n\nPage 19", "First Mint Inauguration: First Mint, LLC, the Company's 100%-owned and operated minting facility in Nevada, USA celebrated its Inauguration on September 26, 2024. W