co.** First Mint, LLC is the minting facility in Nevada owned 100% by First Majestic Silver Corp. [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.100]. The only references to it are in First Majestic's reports in this document set.\n\n**First Mint's PPE in 2023.**\n- First Mint's property, plant and equipment was $1.8 million at year-end 2023. It includes the bullion store and the Nevada minting facility, and it sits in the \"Other\" category [FSMDA-Q2-2024 p.25] [FSMDA-Q1-2024 p.24].\n- It rose to $3.1 million in Q1 2024, $3.4 million in Q2 and $4.1 million in Q3 [FSMDA-Q1-2024 p.24] [FSMDA-Q2-2024 p.25] [FSMDA-Q3-2024 p.25]. That is the only evidence of how an expansion would show up. The growth was recorded as PPE, not as a derecognition.\n- The filings say assets under construction are recorded at cost. They are reallocated to land and buildings, machinery and equipment, or other when they become available for use [FSMDA-Q2-2024 p.24].\n- Depreciation begins once the operating levels management intended have been reached [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.23].\n- Commissioning began in March 2024. The mint added coin presses, lasers and etching equipment, which the company said would raise throughput by more than 50% [FSMDA-Q2-2024 p.66] [FSMDA-Q3-2024 p.65].\n- From 1 January 2024, First Mint became its own reporting segment. Its earlier figures had been in \"Others\" and were restated [FSMDA-Q1-2024 p.11].\n\n**Derecognized mine assets are unrelated to First Mint.**\n- The only derecognition mentioned involves non-operating mines. La Guitarra and La Parrilla were classified as held for sale and disposed of on 29 March 2023 and 14 August 2023 [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.56]. By 31 December 2024 their assets and liabilities had been derecognized (Note 14).\n- Separately, Jerritt Canyon, also in Nevada, was placed on temporary suspension on 20 March 2023. That is a different asset from First Mint. The 2023 impairment of $125.2 million included $29.7 million of PPE [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.50].\n\nNothing in the documents links First Mint's growth to the reclassification of mine assets, or shows a 2023 effect from an expansion.", "expectedOutput": "In 2023, First Mint\u2019s property, plant and equipment (PPE) in Nevada was included in \"Other\" at $51.8 million, but by 2024 this decreased to $3.1 million. Meanwhile, non-producing mines like La Guitarra and La Parrilla were classified as assets held-for-sale until their disposal, after which their assets and liabilities were derecognized as of December 31, 2023. Therefore, if First Mint\u2019s Nevada facilities expand, their PPE would increase and appear in \"Other,\" while derecognized mine assets would not be reflected on the balance sheet, demonstrating a shift from derecognition of sold mines to increased PPE from ongoing Nevada operations.", "context": ["(3) Included in \"Other\" is property, plant and equipment of $3.1 million (2023 51.8 million) for First Mint which includes the Company's bullion store and its minting facility located in Nevada\n\nProperty, plant and equipment, including land and buildings, machinery and equipment; assets under construction and other assets above are allocated by mine as follow:\n\n<invoke name=\"Read\">\n<parameter name=\"file_path\">/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-jmanuelc87-Documents-Companies-Cognitactix-grupo-mexico-evals/dde52c23-b3a0-4425-a3ab-62404ca21536/images/1.png</parameter>\n</invoke>\nalt\n\n\n<invoke name=\"Read\">\n<parameter name=\"file_path\">/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-jmanuelc87-Documents-Companies-Cognitactix-grupo-mexico-evals/dde52c23-b3a0-4425-a3ab-62404ca21536/images/1.png</parameter>\n</invoke>\nalt\n\nTabular amounts are expressed in thousands of US dollars)\n\nPage\n\nNOTES TO CONDENSED INTERIM CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS\n\nFirst Majestic Silver Corp. 2024 First Quarter Report\n\n(1) Non-producing properties include the San Martin, Del Toro, La Parrilla and La Guitarra mines. La Guitarra and La Parrilla were classified as assets held-for- sale up to the date o