\\nTabular amounts are expressed in thousands of US dollars)\\n\\nPage\\n\\nNOTES TO CONDENSED INTERIM CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS\\n\\nFirst Majestic Silver Corp. 2024 First Quarter Report\\n\\n(1) Non-producing properties include the San Martin, Del Toro, La Parrilla and La Guitarra mines. La Guitarra and La Parrilla were classified as assets held-for- sale up to the date of disposition on March 29, 2023 and August 14, 2023, respectively. As of December 31, 2023, the assets and liabilities have been derecognized\\n\\nThe accompanying notes are an integral part of the condensed interim consolidated financial statements\\n\\nCondensed Interim Consolidated Financial Statements Unaudited\\n]", "input": "If First Mint's Nevada facilities expand, how does PPE vs. derecognized mine asset classification shift in 2023?", "actualOutput": "## Short answer\n\nThe documents don't support this scenario \u2014 there is no disclosure of any \"expansion\" of First Mint's Nevada facilities, and even if there were, it could not change the 2023 classification of derecognized mine assets. The two items are unrelated line items, and 2023 is a closed reporting period.\n\n## What the documents actually show\n\n**1. First Mint is a PP&E item, and a very small one**\n\nFirst Mint, LLC is First Majestic's 100%-owned minting facility in Nevada, which vertically integrates bullion production [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.100]. Its assets sit inside the \"Other\" category of Property, Plant and Equipment:\n\n> \"Included in 'Other' is property, plant and equipment of $3.1 million (2023 \u2013 $1.8 million) for First Mint which includes the Company's bullion store and its minting facility located in Nevada\" [FSMDA-Q1-2024 p.24]\n\nSo the only \"shift\" tied to First Mint's build-out was an increase in the Other/PP&E bucket from **$1.8M (2023) to $3.1M (Q1 2024)** \u2014 capitalized as PP&E (land and buildings, machinery and equipment, assets under construction), not reclassified from anything mining-related.\n\nTiming also matters: commissioning and bullion sales only **commenced in March 2024**, and the inauguration was September 26, 2024, with additional coin presses, lasers and etching equipment commissioned in Q4 2024 [FSMDA-Q3-2024 p.54; 2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.82]. In 2023 the mint was not yet operating and was reported within the \"Others\" segment [FSMDA-Q1-2024 p.12].\n\n**2. The 2023 derecognitions are a separate, mine-level divestiture matter**\n\nThe derecognized assets in 2023 relate to divested Mexican mines, not to Nevada:\n\n- La Guitarra and La Parrilla were classified as **assets held-for-sale up to their disposition dates (March 29, 2023 and August 14, 2023)**; \"As of December 31, 2023, the assets and liabilities have been derecognized\" [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.48].\n- On disposition, each asset \"is no longer classified as held-for-sale, with the assets and liabilities derecognized after disposition\" [FSMDA-Q1-2024 p.19].\n- La Guitarra: carrying value at disposal $34.3M, consideration $33.2M, giving a **$1.4M loss on disposition** after a $0.2M working capital adjustment [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.42].\n- La Parrilla's disposal group had a net carrying value of **$56.4M at December 31, 2022**; its liabilities remain with the Company because the sale was an asset purchase agreement [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.76].\n\n## Why the premise doesn't hold\n\nDerecognition under the held-for-sale pathway is driven by the sale of those specific mining interests, while First Mint capex flows into PP&E (and its own reporting segment from Q1 2024). Growth in Nevada minting capacity would increase PP&E/assets under construction prospectively; it would not move mining interests between categories, and it has no bearing on balances already derecognized at December 31, 2023.\n\nIf you are looking for a forward-looking capex or capacity-expansion plan for First Mint, the retrieved passages do not contain one \u2014 only the ISO 9001 certification expected in 2025 [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.82].\n\n**One caveat:** these results come from First Majestic Silver Corp. filings, not Grupo M\u00e9xico reports. If you intended a Grupo M\u00e9xico question, let me know and I'll search accordingly.", "expectedOutput": "In 2023, First Mint\u2019s property, plant and equipment (PPE) in Nevada was included in \"Other\" at $51.8 million, but by 2024 this decreased to $3.1 million. Meanwhile, non-producing mines like La Guitarra and La Parrilla were classified as assets held-for-sale until their disposal, after which their assets and liabilities were derecognized as of December 31, 2023. Therefore, if First Mint\u2019s Nevada facilities expand, their PPE would increase and appear in \"Other,\" while derecognized mine assets would not be reflected on the balance sheet, demonstrating a shift from derecognition of sold mines to increased PPE from ongoing Nevada operations.", "context": ["(3) Included in \"Other\" is property, plant and equipment of $3.1 million (2023 51.8 million) for First Mint which includes the Company's bullion store and its minting facility located in Nevada\n\nProperty, plant and equipment, including land and buildings, machinery and equipment; assets under construction and other assets above are allocated by mine as follow:\n\n<invoke name=\"Read\">\n<parameter name=\"file_path\">/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-jmanuelc87-Documents-Companies-Cognitactix-grupo-mexico-evals/dde52c23-b3a0-4425-a3ab-62404ca21536/images/1.png</parameter>\n</invoke>\nalt\n\n\n<invoke name=\"Read\">\n<parameter name=\"file_path\">/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-jmanuelc87-Documents-Companies-Cognitactix-grupo-mexico-evals/dde52c23-b3a0-4425-a3ab-62404ca21536/images/1.png</parameter>\n</invoke>\nalt\n\nTabular amounts are expressed in thousands of US dollars)\n\nPage\n\nNOTES TO CONDENSED INTERIM CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS\n\nFirst Majestic Silver Corp. 2024 First Quarter Report\n\n(1) Non-producing properties include the San Martin, Del Toro, La Parrilla and La Guitarr