 $(0.17)), compared with $(13.6)M in Q1 2024 and $(17.5)M in Q2 2023 [FSMDA-Q2-2024 p.53, p.76].\n\n**Why the disconnect between operational gains and the bigger net loss?** The quarter's loss was driven by non-operating / non-cash items:\n\n- A **$22.6M non-cash deferred income tax expense** (vs. a $10.3M deferred tax *recovery* in Q2 2023 and a $10.7M recovery in Q1 2024), largely tied to USD strength against the Mexican Peso affecting Mexican tax pools [FSMDA-Q2-2024 p.53, p.72].\n- A **$11.1M non-cash foreign exchange loss** (vs. a $6.0M gain in Q2 2023 and a $1.2M gain in Q1 2024) [FSMDA-Q2-2024 p.53, p.76].\n- Total **income tax expense of $30.5M** in Q2 2024 vs. a $5.0M recovery in Q2 2023 [FSMDA-Q2-2024 p.72].\n\n**Six-month view:** The combined H1 2024 net loss was $61.8M (EPS $(0.21)), an improvement vs. the $118.2M net loss (EPS $(0.43)) in H1 2023 [FSMDA-Q2-2024 p.75].\n\n## Bottom Line\n\nQ2 2024 showed a genuine operational turnaround \u2014 higher revenue vs. Q1 and a meaningful jump in mine operating earnings vs. both Q1 2024 and Q2 2023 \u2014 but the headline net loss nearly quadrupled quarter-over-quarter because of **non-cash tax and FX items** tied to peso/dollar movements, not core operations.\n\nIf you were asking specifically about **Grupo Mexico's own** Q2 financials, those don't appear to be in the indexed documents \u2014 let me know and I can look again with different search terms.", "expectedOutput": "In Q2 2024, revenues increased significantly to $136.2M (up 28% from Q1), driven by operational gains such as a 15% rise in ore processed and higher silver and gold production. However, Q2 also saw a much larger net loss of ($48.3M), up from ($13.6M) in Q1 and ($17.5M) in Q2 last year, indicating that despite improved operations and revenue, costs or other factors significantly impacted profitability compared to both prior quarter and the same quarter last year.", "context": ["2024 SECOND QUARTER HIGHLIGHTS\n\n| Key Performance Metrics | 20