ning right-of-use assets; total lease liabilities (current + NC) fell from $36.7M to $27.5M [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.54].\n- Decommissioning liabilities rose +$7.5M reflecting mine site rehabilitation obligation growth.\n- **Deferred tax liabilities were nearly flat (+$1.1M)** [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.11].\n\n---\n\n## 5. \ud83d\udfe9 DEFERRED TAX ASSETS & LIABILITIES (Deep Dive)\n\nThis is the most notable balance sheet shift. The full movement table [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.58]:\n\n### Deferred Tax Assets (Gross)\n| Component | Dec 31, 2023 | Dec 31, 2024 | Change |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Losses | $202,608 | $238,014 | +$35,406 |\n| Provisions | 42,207 | 44,250 | +2,043 |\n| DTA not recognized | (130,613) | (159,328) | \u221228,715 |\n| Other | 21,818 | 18,858 | \u22122,960 |\n| **Gross DTA** | **$136,020** | **$141,794** | **+$5,774** |\n\n### Deferred Tax Liabilities (Gross)\n| Component | Dec 31, 2023 | Dec 31, 2024 | Change |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| PP&E & mining interests | $129,941 | $188,517 | **+$58,576** |\n| Effect of Mexican tax deconsolidation | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 |\n| Other | (3,637) | (13,004) | \u22129,367 |\n| **Gross DTL** | **$126,304** | **$175,513** | **+$49,209** |\n\n### Balance Sheet Presentation (Net)\n| | Dec 31, 2023 | Dec 31, 2024 | Change |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Deferred tax assets (BS line) | $88,732 | $46,375 | **\u2212$42,357** |\n| Deferred tax liabilities (BS line) | $79,017 | $80,094 | **+$1,077** |\n| **Net deferred tax position** | **(\u2212$9,715)** *(net liability)* | **+$33,719** *(net asset)* | **+$43,434** |\n\n**Interpretation:** Although the *recognized* gross DTA rose modestly (+$5.8M), the recognized DTA on the balance sheet fell sharply by \u2212$42.4M because more deferred tax assets were **offset against deferred tax liabilities** within the same tax jurisdictions. Meanwhile, gross DTLs rose significantly (+$49.2M), mainly from PP&E/mining interest temporary differences. The net effect reversed the position from a net DTL of \u2212$9.7M to a net DTA of +$33.7M [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.58].\n\n---\n\n## 6. \ud83d\udfea EQUITY\n\n| Line Item | Dec 31, 2023 | Dec 31, 2024 | Change | % Chg |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Share capital | $1,879,971 | $1,978,101 | **+$98,130** | **+5.2%** |\n| Equity reserves | 88,025 | 90,028 | +2,003 | +2.3% |\n| Accumulated deficit | (609,876) | (717,058) | **\u2212$107,182** | **\u221217.6%** |\n| **Total Equity** | **$1,358,120** | **$1,351,071** | **\u2212$7,049** | **\u22120.5%** |\n\n**Key drivers:**\n- Share capital rose strongly +$98.1M (+5.2%), driven by new share issuances [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.12].\n- Accumulated deficit deepened by \u2212$107.2M, indicating continued net losses in 2024 (despite higher revenues, heavy depreciation, deferred tax movements, and decommissioning costs weighed on net income).\n- Equity reserves grew modestly +$2.0M (share-based compensation).\n- **Total equity declined only marginally (\u2212$7.0M, \u22120.5%)** as new capital raised nearly offset the deficit expansion [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.11, p.12].\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udcca Summary Scorecard\n\n| Category | Dec 31, 2023 | Dec 31, 2024 | Net Change |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Total Current Assets** | $309,057 | $368,821 | **+$59,764 \u25b2** |\n| **Total Non-Current Assets** | $1,667,298 | $1,610,967 | **\u2212$56,331 \u25bc** |\n| **Total Assets** | $1,976,355 | $1,979,788 | **+$3,433 \u25b2** |\n| **Total Current Liabilities** | $120,138 | $144,307 | **+$24,169 \u25b2** |\n| **Total Non-Current Liabilities** | $498,097 | $484,410 | **\u2212$13,687 \u25bc** |\n| **Total Liabilities** | $618,235 | $628,717 | **+$10,482 \u25b2** |\n| **Total Equity** | $1,358,120 | $1,351,071 | **\u2212$7,049 \u25bc** |\n| **DTA (BS line)** | $88,732 | $46,375 | **\u2212$42,357 \u25bc** |\n| **DTL (BS line)** | $79,017 | $80,094 | **+$1,077 \u25b2** |\n\n**Sources:** [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.11], [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.12], [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.52], [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.54], [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.58]", "expectedOutput": "Between Decem