 by $34.7 M** |\n\nRevenue and mine operating earnings improved sharply QoQ, driven by higher payable AgEq ounces sold and a higher average realized silver price [FSMDA-Q2-2024 p.76]. Yet the net loss deepened from $13.6 M to $48.3 M, primarily due to:\n\n- A $22.6 M deferred income tax *expense* in Q2 vs. a $10.7 M deferred tax *recovery* in Q1.\n- An $11.1 M FX loss in Q2 vs. a $1.2 M FX *gain* in Q1.\n- Partially offset by $1.1 M lower share-based payments [FSMDA-Q2-2024 p.76].\n\n---\n\n### 3. Eight-Quarter Revenue & Profitability Trend\n\n| Quarter | Revenue | Mine Op. Earnings (Loss) | Net (Loss) / Earnings | EPS (basic) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Q1 2023** | $156,952 | ($6,423) | ($100,660) | ($0.37) |\n| **Q2 2023** | $146,692 | $1,138 | ($17,534) | ($0.06) |\n| **Q3 2023** | $133,211 | $13,026 | ($27,149) | ($0.09) |\n| **Q4 2023** | $136,946 | $17,901 | $10,231 | $0.04 |\n| **Q1 2024** | $106,014 | ($321) | ($13,563) | ($0.05) |\n| **Q2 2024** | $136,166 | $15,462 | ($48,251) | ($0.17) |\n| **Q3 2024** | $146,087 | $28,522 | ($26,593) | ($0.09) |\n| **Q4 2024** | $172,337 | $48,237 | ($13,478) | ($0.04) |\n\n[2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.110] [FSMDA-Q1-2024 p.69]\n\n**Observations:**\n\n- **Revenue** hit its lowest point in Q1 2024 ($106 M) then recovered steadily to a multi-quarter high of $172 M in Q4 2024.\n- **Mine operating earnings** show a strong upward trajectory across 2024: ($0.3 M) \u2192 $15.5 M \u2192 $28.5 M \u2192 $48.2 M \u2014 far exceeding any quarter in the 2023 series.\n- **Net losses** tell a different story. Q2 2024 was the worst quarter for net results ($48.3 M loss, or \u2013$0.17/share), despite being the second-best Q2 for mine operating earnings. The disconnect is almost entirely driven by **non-cash items** (deferred taxes and FX).\n- From Q2 2024 onward, net losses progressively narrowed ($48.3 M \u2192 $26.6 M \u2192 $13.5 M), converging with the improving operational picture.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Summary\n\n| Dimension | Q2 2024 Verdict |\n|---|---|\n| **Revenue vs. Q2 2023** | Down 7%, but up 28% vs. the prior quarter (Q1 2024) |\n| **Mine operating earnings** | $15.5 M \u2014 a dramatic improvement over Q2 2023 ($1.1 M) and Q1 2024 (\u2013$0.3 M) |\n| **Net loss** | $48.3 M \u2014 the **deepest quarterly loss in 2024**, despite operational gains, owing to ~$33 M adverse deferred-tax swing and ~$17 M adverse FX swing |\n| **Subsequent trend** | Both operational and net results improved markedly in Q3 and Q4 2024, as FX and tax headwinds eased |\n\nIn short, Q2 2024 illustrates a stark **divergence between operational improvement and bottom-line results**: the mines were generating substantially more earnings, but non-cash deferred tax and foreign-exchange effects more than offset those gains and inflated the net loss to its worst level of the year.", "expectedOutput": "In Q2 2024, revenues increased significantly to $136.2M (up 28% from Q1), driven by operational gains such as a 15% rise in ore processed and higher silver and gold production. However, Q2 also saw a much larger net loss of ($48.3M), up from ($13.6M) in Q1 and ($17.5M) in Q2 last year, indicating that despite improved operations and revenue, costs or other factors significantly impacted profitability compared to both prior quarter and the same quarter last year.", "context": ["2024 SECOND QUARTER HIGHLIGHTS\n\n| Key Performance Metrics | 2024-Q2 | 2024-Q1 | Change Q2 vs Q1 | 2023-Q2 | Change Q2 vs Q2 | 2024-YTD | 2023-YTD | Change |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Operational** | | | | | | | | |\n| Ore Processed / Tonnes Milled | 674,570 | 588,651 | 15% | 733,170 | (8%) | 1,263,221 | 1,579,038 | (20%) |\n| Silver Ounces Produced | 2,104,181 | 1,975,176 | 7% | 2,633,411 | (20%) | 4,079,358 | 5,176,470 | (21%) |\n| Gold Ounces Produced | 39,339 | 35,936 | 9% | 45,022 | (13%) | 75,275 | 105,616 | (29%) |\n| Silver Equivalent Ounces Produced | 5,289,439 | 5,162,283 | 2% | 6,320,971 | (16%) | 10,451,724 | 13,948,076 | (25%) |\