ant point: **the documents in this collection are not about Grupo Mexico in the context of your question**. The search results pertain to **First Majestic Silver Corp.**, a Canadian silver mining company \u2014 not Grupo Mexico. \"First Mint\" is a subsidiary of First Majestic Silver Corp., not of Grupo Mexico.\n\nThat said, here is what the documents reveal about First Mint's Nevada facilities and the related asset classifications:\n\n---\n\n### First Mint's Nevada PPE in 2023\n\n- **First Mint LLC** is First Majestic Silver Corp.'s minting facility in Nevada, United States. It was included within the **\"Other\"** category for PPE in 2023, with a reported value of **$51.8 million** at year-end 2023 [FSMDA-Q3-2024 p.25; FSMDA-Q2-2024 p.25].\n- Starting **January 1, 2024**, First Mint was reclassified from \"Others\" to its **own operating segment**, with prior-period comparative information restated accordingly [FSMDA-Q1-2024 p.11; 2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.35].\n\n### Derecognized Mine Assets in 2023\n\nThe derecognitions that occurred in 2023 were **unrelated to First Mint**. Specifically:\n- **La Guitarra** and **La Parrilla** mines were classified as assets held-for-sale and disposed of on March 29, 2023 and August 14, 2023, respectively. As of December 31, 2023, their assets and liabilities were **derecognized** [FSMDA-Q3-2024 p.21; FSMDA-Q1-2024 p.20].\n\n### No Hypothetical \"Expansion Shift\" Addressed\n\nThe documents **do not discuss any hypothetical scenario** in which First Mint's Nevada facilities expand and thereby cause a shift in PPE vs. derecognized mine asset classification. The 2023 derecognitions (La Guitarra and La Parrilla) and First Mint's PPE are treated as entirely separate line items, and there is no indication in the filings that one affects the other.\n\n---\n\n**In summary**, the available documents do not contain information about a classification shift between PPE and derecognized mine assets driven by a First Mint expansion. The question appears to be based on a hypothetical scenario not addressed in the filings.", "expectedOutput": "In 2023, First Mint\u2019s property, plant and equipment (PPE) in Nevada was included in \"Other\" at $51.8 million, but by 2024 this decreased to $3.1 million. Meanwhile, non-producing mines like La Guitarra and La Parrilla were classified as assets held-for-sale until their disposal, after which their assets and liabilities were derecognized as of December 31, 2023. Therefore, if First Mint\u2019s Nevada facilities expand, their PPE would increase and appear in \"Other,\" while derecognized mine assets would not be reflected on the balance sheet, demonstrating a shift from derecognition of sold mines to increased PPE from ongoing Nevada operations.", "context": ["(3) Included in \"Other\" is property, plant and equipment of $3.1 million (2023 51.8 million) for First Mint which includes the Company's bullion store and its minting facility located in Nevada\n\nProperty, plant and equipment, including land and buildings, machinery and equipment; assets under construction and other assets above are allocated by mine as follow:\n\n<invoke name=\"Read\">\n<parameter name=\"file_path\">/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-jmanuelc87-Documents-Companies-Cognitactix-grupo-mexico-evals/dde52c23-b3a0-4425-a3ab-62404ca21536/images/1.png</parameter>\n</invoke>\nalt\n\n\n<invoke name=\"Read\">\n<parameter name=\"file_path\">/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-jmanuelc87-Documents-Companies-Cognitactix-grupo-mexico-evals/dde52c23-b3a0-4425-a3ab-62404ca21536/images/1.png</parameter>\n</invoke>\nalt\n\nTabular amounts are expressed in thousands of US dollars)\n\nPage\n\nNOTES TO CONDENSED INTERIM CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS\n\nFirst Majestic Silver Corp. 2024 First Quarter Report\n\n(1) Non-producing properties include the San Martin, Del Toro, La Parrilla and La Guitarra mines. La Guitarra and La Parrilla were classified as assets held-for- sale up to the date of disposition on March 29, 2023