31, 2023\\n\\nPage\\n\\nFirst Majestic Silver Corp. 2024 Second Quarter Report\\n\\nThe accompanying notes are an integral part of the condensed interim consolidated financial statements\\n]", "input": "How would a major asset sale in Q2 2024 affect assets, liabilities, and equity compared to prior periods?", "actualOutput": "Based on the provided financial statements and reports, **no major asset sale took place in Q2 2024**:\n\n1. **No Q2 2024 Divestiture**: Note 14 (*Divestitures*) in the Q2 2024 report only details transactions completed in prior periods in 2023 (the sale of the La Guitarra mine in March 2023 and the La Parrilla mine in August 2023) [FSMDA-Q2-2024 p.19-20]. The investing cash flows for the six months ended June 30, 2024 reflect ordinary capital expenditures and exploration, with only minor proceeds from the disposal of marketable securities ($11.8 million), rather than a major asset sale [FSMDA-Q2-2024 p.6, p.77]. Likewise, Grupo M\u00e9xico's sustainability reports do not report any major asset sale in Q2 2024 [IDS24_ESP_06_Ambiental_ebook p.143].\n\n---\n\n### Accounting Impact of a Major Asset Sale Compared to Prior Periods\nBased on the accounting policies and past divestiture disclosures set out in the financial reports [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.33, p.42, p.76; FSMDA-Q2-2024 p.19-20], a major asset sale affects assets, liabilities, and equity as follows:\n\n* **Assets:**\n  * *Prior to completion (Held for Sale):* If a disposal is highly probable, non-current assets (e.g., property, plant, and equipment; mining interests) are reclassified to current assets as *\"assets held-for-sale\"* at the lower of carrying value and fair value less costs to sell (FVLCTS), and depreciation ceases [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.33, p.42].\n  * *Upon completion (Sale):* The carrying value of the disposed asset is derecognized from the balance sheet. In exchange, the consideration received (e.g., cash and cash equivalents, or marketable securities/equity shares) is recognized in current or non-current financial assets [FSMDA-Q2-2024 p.19-20].\n* **Liabilities:**\n  * *Disposal group liabilities:* Any liabilities directly associated with the assets sold are reclassified as current *\"liabilities held-for-sale\"* prior to closing [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.42].\n  * *Upon disposition:* If the transaction is structured as a share sale or the buyer assumes the liabilities, those liabilities are derecognized. If it is an asset purchase agreement where the seller retains liabilities, those liabilities remain on the balance sheet [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.76].\n* **Equity:**\n  * *Gain or loss on disposal:* The difference between the total net consideration received (adjusted for transaction costs and working capital) and the net carrying value of the derecognized assets and liabilities is recognized as an operating gain or loss in the statement of earnings [FSMDA-Q2-2024 p.19].\n  * *Impact on retained earnings:* This net gain or loss flows directly into retained earnings (accumulated deficit) within shareholders' equity [FSMDA-Q2-2024 p.8, p.19].", "expectedOutput": "A major asset sale in Q2 2024 would decrease total assets due to the removal of the sold asset. Depending on how the proceeds are used, liabilities may decrease if debts are paid off, or cash may increase if retained. Equity could increase if the asset is sold for more than its carrying value, resulting in a gain, or decrease in case of a loss. These changes would be reflected in the Condensed Interim Consolidated Statements of Financial Position as at June 30, 2024.", "context": ["<invoke name=\"noop\">\n</invoke>\n\nThe Condensed Interim Consolidated Statements of Financial Position provides a summary of assets, liabilities and equity, as vell as their current versus non-current nature as at the reporting date.\n\nAS AI JUNE 30, 2024 AND DECEMBER 31, 2023\n\nPage\n\nFirst Majestic Silver Corp. 2024 Second Quarter Report\n\nThe accompanying notes are an integral part of the condensed interim cons