c23-b3a0-4425-a3ab-62404ca21536/images/1.png</parameter>\\n</invoke>\\nalt\\n\\nTabular amounts are expressed in thousands of US dollars)\\n\\nPage\\n\\nNOTES TO CONDENSED INTERIM CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS\\n\\nFirst Majestic Silver Corp. 2024 First Quarter Report\\n\\n(1) Non-producing properties include the San Martin, Del Toro, La Parrilla and La Guitarra mines. La Guitarra and La Parrilla were classified as assets held-for- sale up to the date of disposition on March 29, 2023 and August 14, 2023, respectively. As of December 31, 2023, the assets and liabilities have been derecognized\\n\\nThe accompanying notes are an integral part of the condensed interim consolidated financial statements\\n\\nCondensed Interim Consolidated Financial Statements Unaudited\\n]", "input": "If First Mint's Nevada facilities expand, how does PPE vs. derecognized mine asset classification shift in 2023?", "actualOutput": "Based on the financial reports of First Majestic Silver Corp., an expansion of First Mint\u2019s Nevada facilities does **not shift or alter the classification between Property, Plant and Equipment (PPE) and derecognized mine assets from 2023**. \n\n### 1. Classification of First Mint's Nevada Facilities\n* **First Mint, LLC** is a 100%-owned minting facility located in Nevada, vertically integrating bullion manufacturing (commissioning commenced in March 2024, followed by its formal inauguration in September 2024) [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.100].\n* Any expansion, construction, or equipment installations (such as flameless tunnels, coin presses, laser/etching equipment) are classified and capitalized under **Property, Plant and Equipment (IAS 16)** (e.g., *Assets under Construction*, *Machinery and Equipment*, or *Land and Buildings*) [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.20, p.47; FSMDA-Q3-2024 p.54, p.65].\n\n### 2. Mine Asset Derecognition in 2023\n* In 2023, derecognized mine assets consisted of non-producing mining properties that were classified as **assets held-for-sale** and then completely removed from the balance sheet upon the completion of their disposition:\n  * **La Guitarra Silver Mine** (disposed March 29, 2023) [FSMDA-Q1-2024 p.20].\n  * **La Parrilla Silver Mine** (disposed August 14, 2023) [FSMDA-Q1-2024 p.20; 2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.76].\n* As of December 31, 2023, the assets and liabilities of these mines were derecognized entirely [FSMDA-Q1-2024 p.20; 2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.76].\n* *(Note: The Jerritt Canyon gold mine in Nevada was placed on temporary suspension in March 2023 and subjected to an impairment charge, but it was not derecognized [FSMDA-Q1-2024 p.25; FSMDA-Q3-2024 p.27]).*\n\n### 3. Impact on Classification\n* Under IFRS accounting standards, **derecognition** is the final removal of an asset from the statement of financial position following disposal. \n* There is no mechanism or reporting shift where expanding First Mint's Nevada facility reclassifies or offsets previously derecognized mine assets; new investments in First Mint remain additions to **PPE**, completely independent of 2023 derecognitions.", "expectedOutput": "In 2023, First Mint\u2019s property, plant and equipment (PPE) in Nevada was included in \"Other\" at $51.8 million, but by 2024 this decreased to $3.1 million. Meanwhile, non-producing mines like La Guitarra and La Parrilla were classified as assets held-for-sale until their disposal, after which their assets and liabilities were derecognized as of December 31, 2023. Therefore, if First Mint\u2019s Nevada facilities expand, their PPE would increase and appear in \"Other,\" while derecognized mine assets would not be reflected on the balance sheet, demonstrating a shift from derecognition of sold mines to increased PPE from ongoing Nevada operations.", "context": ["(3) Included in \"Other\" is property, plant and equipment of $3.1 million (2023 51.8 million) for First Mint which includes the Company's bullion store and its minting facility located in Nevada\n\nProperty, plant and equipment, including land