ate.\\n\\nAS AI JUNE 30, 2024 AND DECEMBER 31, 2023\\n\\nPage\\n\\nFirst Majestic Silver Corp. 2024 Second Quarter Report\\n\\nThe accompanying notes are an integral part of the condensed interim consolidated financial statements\\n]", "input": "How would a major asset sale in Q2 2024 affect assets, liabilities, and equity compared to prior periods?", "actualOutput": "Based on the financial statement policies and balance sheet accounting standards reported in the company's financial reports [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.33, FSMDA-Q2-2024 p.19], a major asset sale in Q2 2024 would impact **Assets**, **Liabilities**, and **Equity** compared to prior periods through the following mechanics:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Pre-Sale Classification (Assets and Liabilities Held for Sale)\nBefore the sale closes, if the transaction meets IFRS criteria as a highly probable sale:\n* **Current vs. Non-Current Assets:** The carrying value of the non-current asset or disposal group is reclassified from non-current assets (e.g., Property, Plant & Equipment or Mining Interests) to **Current Assets** as *\"Assets held for sale\"* [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.33, 42].\n* **Current Liabilities:** Any liabilities directly associated with the asset/disposal group are reclassified to **Current Liabilities** as *\"Liabilities held for sale\"* [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.42].\n* **Depreciation:** Non-current assets cease being depreciated once classified as held for sale [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.33].\n* **Valuation / Impairment:** Held-for-sale assets are measured at the lower of carrying value and Fair Value Less Costs to Sell (FVLCTS). Any excess of carrying value over FVLCTS is immediately recognized as an impairment loss in net earnings, reducing **Equity** prior to closing [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.33].\n\n---\n\n### 2. Impact on Assets\nUpon closing of the sale:\n* **Derecognition:** Non-current assets (or assets held for sale) are removed (derecognized) from the balance sheet [FSMDA-Q2-2024 p.24\u201325].\n* **Cash / Receivables Inflow:** Cash and cash equivalents (or trade/other financial receivables) increase by the net consideration received [FSMDA-Q2-2024 p.19, 2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.111].\n* **Net Change in Total Assets:**\n  * **Sold at a Gain:** Cash received exceeds the net carrying value, resulting in a **net increase in total assets**.\n  * **Sold at a Loss:** Cash received is less than the carrying value, resulting in a **net decrease in total assets** [FSMDA-Q2-2024 p.19].\n  * **Sold at Carrying Value:** Total assets remain unchanged (an asset swap from long-term assets to cash).\n\n---\n\n### 3. Impact on Liabilities\n* **Transfer of Associated Obligations:** If the sold asset or operating unit carries associated liabilities (such as decommissioning obligations, lease liabilities, or vendor payables), those obligations are derecognized upon transfer, leading to a **net reduction in total liabilities** [2024-Q4-FS-MDA p.33, 42].\n* **Debt Paydown:** If management uses the cash proceeds to pay down short-term or long-term debt facilities, current or non-current debt liabilities decrease alongside cash [FSMDA-Q2-2024 p.29].\n\n---\n\n### 4. Impact on Equity\n* **Gain or Loss on Disposition:** The net gain or loss on sale (calculated as total net consideration minus net carrying value and transaction costs/working capital adjustments) is recognized on the Income Statement [FSMDA-Q2-2024 p.19].\n* **Retained Earnings:** \n  * A **gain on sale** increases net income and flows into Retained Earnings, **increasing total Equity** relative to prior periods.\n  * A **loss on sale** decreases net income and Retained Earnings, **reducing total Equity** relative to prior periods [FSMDA-Q2-2024 p.19].\n\n---\n\n### Note on Q2 2024 Financial Reporting\nWhile the Q2 2024 interim reports reflect routine transfers and minor property, plant, and equipment disposals ($2.49 million in accumulated depreciation adjustments) [FSMDA-Q2-2024 p.24\u201325], the notes do not record a new major standalone asset divestiture completed specifically during Q2 2024 itself (earlier divestitures referenced include the sale of the La Guitarra mine completed in March 2023) [FSMDA-Q2-2024 p.19].", "expectedOutput": "A major asset sale in Q2 2024 would decrease total assets due to the removal of the sold asset. Depending on how the proceeds are used, liabilities may decrease if debts are paid off, or cash may increase if retained. Equity could increase if the asset is sold for more than its carrying value, resulting in a gain, or decrease in case of a loss. These changes would be reflected in the Condensed Interim Consolidated Statements of Financial Position as at June 30, 2024.", "context": ["<invoke name=\"noop\">\n</invoke>\n\nThe Condensed Interim Consolidated Statements of Financial Position provides a summary of assets, liabilities and equity, as vell as their current versus non-current nature as at the reporting date.\n\nAS AI JUNE 30, 2024 AND DECEMBER 31, 2023\n\nPage\n\nFirst Majestic Silver Corp. 2024 Second Quarter Report\n\nThe accompanying notes are an integral part of the condensed interim consolidated financial statements\n"], "retrievalContext": ["the transaction was subject to customary closing conditions, including completion of such financing and receipt of all necessary regulatory approvals (which were obtained in May 2023). At March 31, 2023, the sale continued to be considered highly probable; therefore the assets and liabilities were presented as assets and liabilities held for sale and presented separately under current assets and current liabilities.", "to customary closing conditions, including completion of such financing and receipt of all necessary regulatory approvals (which were obtained in May 2023) . At March 31, 2023, the sale continued to be considered highly probable; therefore the assets and liabilities were presented as assets and liabilities held for sale and presented separately under current assets and current liabilities _", "to customary closing conditi