24.\n\n### 1. PPE Classification Shift (First Mint)\nDue to the expansion and increased operational significance of First Mint LLC (a minting facility in Nevada), the company added it as a **significant operating segment** as of January 1, 2024 [FSMDA-Q1-2024 p.11].\n*   **Prior to the Shift:** Property, plant, and equipment (PPE) and operating results for First Mint were previously grouped within the **\"Others\"** segment [FSMDA-Q1-2024 p.11].\n*   **2023 Restatement:** For the 2024 reporting periods, the 2023 comparative information was shifted so that First Mint's PPE\u2014which was **$1.8 million** at December 31, 2023\u2014is now reported separately under the First Mint segment rather than in \"Others\" [FSMDA-Q3-2024 p.11, 25].\n\n### 2. Derecognized Mine Asset Classification\nSimultaneously, the 2023 fiscal year saw a major shift in \"Mining Interests\" due to the disposal of non-producing properties:\n*   **Derecognition:** The assets and liabilities of the **La Guitarra** and **La Parrilla** mines were **derecognized** as of December 31, 2023 [FSMDA-Q1-2024 p.20].\n*   **Timing:** These mines were classified as \"assets held-for-sale\" until their respective dispositions on March 29, 2023, and August 14, 2023. By the end of 2023, they were removed from the balance sheet entirely, contrasting with the PPE of the First Mint facility, which remains an active part of the consolidated PPE [FSMDA-Q1-2024 p.20].\n\n### Summary of the 2023 Shift\nIn the 2023 comparative columns of the 2024 reports, the classification shifted by **extracting First Mint's PPE from \"Others\"** to its own segment, while **removing the derecognized mine assets** (La Guitarra and La Parrilla) from the \"Mining Interests\" and \"Non-producing Properties\" categories following their sale [FSMDA-Q1-2024 p.11, 20].\n\nSources:\n* [FSMDA-Q1-2024 p.11, 20]\n* [FSMDA-Q3-2024 p.11, 25]", "expectedOutput": "In 2023, First Mint\u2019s property, plant and equipment (PPE) in Nevada was included in